# Lesson 2, new hand: partner opens a strong two-bid and you have almost nothing.
title: Partner opens 2♠: you must bid
id: L02-21
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.5, 2.7
student: S
board: 21
dealer: N
vulnerable: NS

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  AKQJ74 AK5    AK3    8
  E  3      JT87   962    KJ753
  S  85     Q962   J874   T62
  W  T962   43     QT5    AQ94

auction:
  N 2S     = 22+ points, five or more spades: forcing
  E Pass
  S 2NT*   = The waiting response: tells partner nothing yet
     key: Partner's 2♠ is forcing, so you must bid even with 3 points. 2NT keeps the auction open and lets partner describe her hand.
     not Pass: Partner's 2♠ is forcing. Did you remember you must bid once?
     not 3S: Is two small spades enough to raise?
     not 3H: To bid your own suit you need a pretty good hand and a good suit. Is that this hand?
     not *: When partner's bid is forcing, which response is almost always right?
  W Pass
  N 4S     = Game in spades
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = Partner has chosen the game
     key: Partner knows you may have nothing and still chose 4♠. Pass.
     not *: Partner knows you may have nothing and still chose 4♠. Is there anything left to say?
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Partner's 2♠ showed 22 or more points and at least five spades, and it
  was forcing: you had to bid. 2NT is the waiting bid. It says nothing
  about your hand, so partner, knowing you might have nothing, still bid
  game with her strong hand and long spades. North is declarer, because
  she bid spades first, and so East will lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E HJ  S H2  W H3  N HK
  2   N SA  E S3  S S5  W S2
      note: Declarer's plan: draw trumps, then play hearts for four tricks to get rid of the club loser. Start drawing trumps.
  3   N SK  E C3  S S8  W S6
      note: Keep drawing trumps.
  4   N SQ  E D2  S C2  W S9
      note: West still has trumps.
  5   N SJ  E C5  S C6  W ST
      note: The last trump is gone.
  6   N HA  E H7  S H6  W H4
      note: Now the hearts.
  7   N H5  E H8  S H9  W C4
      note: A heart to dummy.
  8   S HQ  W C9  N C8  E HT
      note: Dummy's ♥Q lets declarer get rid of the club loser.
  9   S D4  W D5  N DK  E D6
      note: A diamond to declarer's ♦K.
  10  N S7  E C7  S D7  W CQ
      note: Declarer's trumps are winners.
  11  N S4  E CJ  S D8  W CA
      note: Another trump.
  12  N DA  E D9  S DJ  W DT
      note: The ♦A.
  13  N D3  E CK  S CT  W DQ
      note: West's ♦Q takes the last trick. 12 tricks: 4♠ made with two overtricks.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: draw trumps, then play hearts for four tricks to get
  rid of the club loser.

  4♠ made with two overtricks. Your ♥Q was worth a trick, but partner bid
  game knowing you might have nothing at all. Your job was simply to keep
  the auction open.
